fsck - check a Project9 ext2 partition

SYNOPSIS
    fsck [-y] device

DESCRIPTION
    Check an unmounted single-group ext2 partition, such as hd1p1
    on a test installer disk. The -y option rebuilds the allocation
    bitmaps and free counts after the inode and directory checks pass.

    To check an ext2 image from the build host, stop the guest and
    run python3 tools/installimage.py --check path/to/disk.img.

EXIT STATUS
    0   The filesystem is clean.
    1   The filesystem contains an inconsistency or could not be read.
    2   Invalid usage or unsupported partition layout.

SEE ALSO
    stability(1)
